# Line-ending policy.
#
# Deliberately narrow: only the files whose line endings actually change how
# something behaves. There is no repo-wide `* text=auto eol=lf` here, because
# gradle-wrapper.properties and app/proguard-rules.pro are stored with CRLF
# today and a blanket rule would renormalise them for no benefit.

# Runs under /bin/sh on the CI runner. A CRLF checkout — which is what a clone
# with core.autocrlf=true produces — fails as "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M".
# Pin it so no one's local Git config can break the build.
gradlew  text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf

# Windows-only, and stored with CRLF. Keep it that way.
gradlew.bat  text eol=crlf
*.bat        text eol=crlf

# Never apply text conversion to binaries.
*.jar   binary
*.webp  binary
*.png   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.pbf   binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks   binary
